## Why is it important to track your finances?

![[2ec1d6e0c346d9f9247be26d53544f8a_MD5.png]]

importance of finance tarcking

Tracking finances may seem like a no-brainer, but it can easily fall by the wayside for time-crunched small business owners. That can be disastrous for your business — both now and in the future. Finance tracking reduces the time it takes to prepare for taxes and allows you to identify potential issues quickly, which keeps employees honest. Financial tracking is vital to identifying [profitable growth opportunities](https://www.business.com/articles/small-business-profitable-growth/), [creating an exit strategy for businesses](https://www.business.com/articles/business-exit-strategy/) that aren’t performing well and managing expenses.

